  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation Mainstreaming Employment into Sustainable Trade (OLD)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contract related to: Mainstreaming Employment into Sustainable Trade (OLD) - It aims to contribute to decent job creation through sustainable trade i.e. supporting sustainable development by taking into account the social, economic, and environmental dimensions of trade in the Southern Neighbourhood. In order to achieve this, the approach is two-fold: firstly, support the development and implementation of trade and investment policies that factor in job creation. Secondly, promote digital trade and e-commerce to enhance new business opportunities and promote regional economic integration in the Southern Neighbourhood. It contributes to the priorities identified during the UfM Trade, as well as Employment and Labour Ministerial meetings, capitalises on the recommendations of the OECD-UfM study on regional integration, and supports the implementation of the regional Team Europe Initiative (TEI) on &#xbf;Jobs through trade and investment&#xbf;.</narrative>
  </description>
